summary:
  The podcast advance does not stand down inside a stop's fade, so pressing Stop
  in an episode's last seconds starts the next one.

history:
  stopWithFade leaves a short fade window, and onErrorOccurred already refuses
  to act inside it — "the dying stream's last word, not a reason to resurrect
  it". onMediaStatusChanged carried no such line, so an EndOfMedia landing in
  that window ran the advance: the up-next head, or with continuous listening
  on by default the show's oldest unheard download. The sleep timer and a
  headset's Stop reach the same fade. The asymmetry between the two handlers
  was the whole bug. Found 2026-09-14, chasing issue #13.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
                      if (!fadeOutAnimation.running && !root._podPlayUpNextHead()

replace:
                      if (!root._podPlayUpNextHead()

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_a_stop_in_an_episodes_last_seconds_starts_nothing.
  Line-neutral.
